# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `scripts/hooks/*` are `sh` scripts, and this machine
# has core.autocrlf enabled: without this file they check out with CRLF, the
# shebang becomes "#!/bin/sh\r", and the hook fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" -- on Linux always, and on Git Bash often.
# BP-ADR-0016 depends on those hooks actually running.
#
# LF everywhere is also the right default for a Rust project targeting
# Windows and Linux (BP-ADR-0001). PowerShell 7, rustc and cargo all handle
# LF sources without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
